<IndepValue>Coupling 8x8 case\8x8_array_touchstone.s64p\Eqns\VarBlock\F</IndepValue></Item>
<Item XName="ZPORT" Type="Variable">
<Data><T>Array_Cplx64</T><D>2;128;1;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;;914;</D></Data>
<IndepValue>Coupling 8x8 case\8x8_array_touchstone.s64p\Eqns\VarBlock\F</IndepValue>
<Unit><T>Int</T><D>2000</D></Unit></Item></Item></Item>
<Item XName="Font" Type="Font">
<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item></Item>
<Item XName="About_coupling" UserName="About_coupling" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;About Element-to-Element Coupling&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;In an NxN matrix of array elements, the &quot;&lt;STRONG&gt;ArrayCoupling_M&lt;/STRONG&gt;&quot; matrix allows you to specify the coupling coefficients from every element to every other element.&amp;nbsp; For an 8x8 rectangular array, this is&amp;nbsp;a 64x64 mathematical matrix.&amp;nbsp; In Dataflow, this coefficient has no physical basis, it is strictly a matrix operation.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;However, the coefficients can be harvested from an S-parameter matrix of the driving point impedances of the antenna manifold in an EM simulator.&amp;nbsp; In this example, an 8x8 array of microstrip patches was solved in Keysight Momentum, and then exported to an .SNP file.&amp;nbsp; This file was imported into this workspace, and the off-diagonal elements converted to the coefficients needed for this Dataflow analysis.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;BR&gt;This allows the coupling to have a more physical basis.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="NotesDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;e}14;Ro14</D></DVport>
<PVPort><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;dFV{yvZSx24;V}{zxt}{l24</D></PVPort>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<ShowCmd><T>Int</T><D>1</D></ShowCmd>
<Window><T>Array_I64</T><D>1;4;K2;I2;6F;RA</D></Window>
<ZOrder><T>Int</T><D>4</D></ZOrder></Item></Item></Item>
